  "scope": "The seven frozen active media recipes contain one typed native component chain (Krea text encoder, transformer and VAE) and six single-model bindings. Child manifests preserve the exact native parent file identities, roles and ordinals; profile and compiled typed stage order are unchanged. A new direct prepare/integrate/decode acquisition on the identical frozen Krea request produces the exact complete PNG from the retained compiled-recipe run. This tests routing equivalence using the same production numerical implementation, not an independent full-model numerical oracle. No learned representation bridge, projector, adapter or arbitrary component substitution occurs in these recipes; the separate Wan composite-generation bridge experiment is not required by this inventory and no bridge promotion is claimed. Measurements retain original acquisition scopes and do not establish a speedup. Krea visual limitations and partial native numerical checks remain in the image bundle. The initial 3.252-second acceptance failed because its dependency-role check omitted SenseNova's existing flow-profile role; the corrected check retains that exact profile identity and the failure receipt. No generation was repeated. A second 3.268-second verification failed because it called identity validation directly on a decoded environment body whose identity field is intentionally not serialized. The corrected check reconstructs that identity through NewEnvironment. Both verification failures are retained; the acquisition is unchanged.",
